AGVN Player: on Android, PhysFS reads PHYSFS_init's argv0 as a PHYSFS_AndroidInit* (JNIEnv and Context), and SDL's
argv[0] there is the text "app_process": every game crashed (SIGSEGV) before it read a file. Pass NULL on Android;
PhysFS then takes "/" as its base dir, which mkxp-z never uses. Elsewhere nothing changes.

diff --git a/src/filesystem/filesystem.cpp b/src/filesystem/filesystem.cpp
index 67c9be0..3d98a81 100644
--- a/src/filesystem/filesystem.cpp
+++ b/src/filesystem/filesystem.cpp
@@ -295,6 +295,13 @@ static void throwPhysfsError(const char *desc) {
 }
 
 FileSystem::FileSystem(const char *argv0, bool allowSymlinks) {
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+  /* AGVN Player: PhysFS on Android reads argv0 as a PHYSFS_AndroidInit*
+   * (JNIEnv and Context). SDL's argv[0] is the text "app_process", which
+   * PhysFS would read as pointers. NULL gives the base dir "/"; nothing
+   * here uses it, as the game folder and RTPs are mounted by their paths. */
+  argv0 = NULL;
+#endif
   if (PHYSFS_init(argv0) == 0)
     throwPhysfsError("Error initializing PhysFS");
 
